                "text": "**Analyzing Initial Positions**\n\nOkay, I've got two data points: a 7 (orange) and an 8 (teal). Train 1 places 8 at (1, 7) and 7 at (3, 6). The output is peculiar; row 1 is mostly 8s, with a 2 at column 6, and row 3 is mostly 7s, also with a 2 at column 7. Column 6 contains... something. Need to dissect this structure more.\n\n\n**Unveiling Cross-Points**\n\nI've made a breakthrough! Each data point seems to generate horizontal and vertical lines of its own value. The crucial insight is the intersection. Where the horizontal line of one value crosses the vertical line of the other, that's where we get the \"2.\" The initial points, where their own lines intersect, maintain their original values.\n\n\n",
